    "case.negApp.video11": "Screen recording of the app prototype on a phone: scrolling the home screen with programme cards grouped by city, then the filters screen with course fee, start date and rating.",
    "case.negApp.facts": [{"label": "Client", "value": "The Netherlands Education Group, Utrecht"}, {"label": "Platform", "value": "iOS app"}, {"label": "Role", "value": "Sole designer in the company: UX/UI, visual identity, content and website development."}, {"label": "Period", "value": "June 2020 — December 2021 (1.5 years)"}, {"label": "Outcome", "value": "The project was approved by stakeholders and handed over to development."}],
    "case.negApp.sec01.title": "About the project",
    "case.negApp.sec01.body": ["The Netherlands Education Group is a private business school in Utrecht. By the end of my time there I had fully redesigned its website. The next step was a mobile app, which I designed on my own initiative: find and choose a short-term course in Amsterdam, The Hague, Vienna or online, then apply and pay without leaving the app.", "The school's core audience is students, university graduates and young professionals. Choosing a course abroad takes them a lot of time and effort, and they want the whole experience to feel seamless, intuitive and simple."],
    "case.negApp.sec02.title": "Process",
    "case.negApp.sec02.body": ["I went through the full path from goal statement to prototype: user and competitor research, persona and JTBD, use cases, a customer journey map and information architecture, then sketches and wireframes, a style guide and UI kit, visual design and an interactive prototype."],
    "case.negApp.sec03.title": "Research",
    "case.negApp.sec03.body": ["The research is based on the audience of the redesigned website as of 2021. It splits into four segments:"],
    "case.negApp.sec03.list": ["40% — students and graduates aged 21–30 from Asia and Africa", "30% — students and graduates aged 21–30 from Eastern Europe and the CIS", "20% — professionals aged 25–35 from Asia, Africa and the CIS looking for professional courses in the EU", "10% — students and graduates aged 21–30 from the EU and the Americas"],
    "case.negApp.sec04.title": "Persona",
    "case.negApp.sec04.body": ["My primary user is Radja, 21, from Delhi, a marketing student at a state university."],
    "case.negApp.sec04.facts": ["Languages: English and German", "Family: single, no children", "Finances: financially dependent on parents; average monthly family income is €4,000", "How he searches for courses: mostly on an iPhone 11, in the cafeteria and after classes", "Device proficiency: intermediate", "Goal: build a career abroad"],
    "case.negApp.sec04.columns": [{"title": "Goals", "lines": ["Find a course in the EU", "Apply for a course", "Pay for it"]}, {"title": "Fears", "lines": ["Wasting time", "Getting confused", "Inconvenient payment options"]}],
    "case.negApp.sec05.title": "Scenario",
    "case.negApp.sec05.body": ["Situation. Radja studies marketing at a prestigious university and plans to move abroad to build a career. At lunch he has an hour to sit calmly with his phone.", "Motivation. He wants to pick a useful course in the EU, learn all the details and apply easily.", "Outcome. Radja goes abroad on the programme he needs and doesn't spend time on phone calls, bank visits and money transfers."],
    "case.negApp.sec06.title": "User journey",
    "case.negApp.sec06.body": ["I broke down Radja's journey, from discovering the app to registration confirmation, into six stages. For each stage: what he does, thinks and feels, which touchpoints he goes through and where it can be improved."],
    "case.negApp.sec07.title": "Architecture",
    "case.negApp.sec07.body": ["The app starts with onboarding, after which users can sign in, sign up, log in via SMS or continue as a guest. The home screen brings together search with filters and programme collections by city; from any collection the path leads to the course card, application, payment and confirmation, while the tab bar gives access to favourites, help and profile."],
    "case.negApp.sec08.title": "Wireframes",
    "case.negApp.sec08.body": ["Before moving to Figma, I sketched the key screens by hand on paper: sign-in, home, programme lists, the application form, payment and profile."],
    "case.negApp.sec09.title": "Style guide",
    "case.negApp.sec09.body": ["For the interface I put together a style guide: palette, typography in Inter and SF Pro Display, button states, navigation elements and components — tags, icons, the app icon and a push notification."],
    "case.negApp.sec10.title": "Visual design",
    "case.negApp.sec10.body": ["The final screens cover the whole journey: onboarding, sign-in and home, filters, the course card, application and payment, plus favourites, help with FAQ and chat, and profile."],
    "case.negApp.alt01": "Cover: The Netherlands Education Group logo, a short description of the iOS app and two phones with the app, followed by \"What is this project about?\" with a photo of a person holding a phone",
    "case.negApp.alt02": "Design process diagram in five stages, from goal statement and user research to visual design and an interactive prototype",
    "case.negApp.alt03": "Website user research: four donut charts with audience shares of 40%, 30%, 20% and 10% by age, occupation and region",
    "case.negApp.alt04": "Persona Radja, a 21-year-old marketing student from Delhi, with his traits, goals and fears",
    "case.negApp.alt05": "Jobs to be done for Radja: situation, motivation and outcome, with sketch-style icons",
    "case.negApp.alt06": "Customer journey map in two parts, from becoming aware of the app to registration confirmation",
    "case.negApp.alt07": "Information architecture of the app: from launch screen and onboarding to home, programme lists, application, payment and the tab bar sections",
    "case.negApp.alt08": "Photo of paper low-fidelity iOS wireframes with hand-drawn screens: login, home, programme lists, application form, payment and profile",
    "case.negApp.alt09": "Style guide: colour palette, Inter and SF Pro Display type styles, buttons, tab bar, tags, icons, app icon and a push notification",
